,"varisian"]},"level":{"value":10},"privateNotes":"","publicNotes":"","publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Shadows at Sundown"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"perception":{"details":"","mod":18,"senses":[]},"resources":{},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":13},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":15},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":18}},"skills":{"deception":{"base":22},"diplomacy":{"base":18},"medicine":{"base":20},"religion":{"base":18},"society":{"base":17}},"spellcasting":{"rituals":{"dc":29}},"traits":{"rarity":"unique","size":{"value":"med"},"value":["evil","human","humanoid"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"npc","effects":[]},{"_id":"sEss0ea0kYrkkti8","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/npc.svg","items":["aYSZgK07zzoQnxWn","lSsVkgG4wvcHzKAh","8ValGHchQeHCwwNl","tlR6oBCqxaWFJ32D","XTTruu95i7bofgzb","LpVAGWjm0wMwDoSP","8tj61TP8OJy6JNuV","4ejGKi9IAdzmlYSw","mlPi10R2hU6H5D5X","I8kdmPy6Ith6x1V1","1uEk4pIL4rya0iV9"],"name":"Loreavor","system":{"abilities":{"cha":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":6},"str":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":4}},"attributes":{"ac":{"details":"","value":28},"allSaves":{"value":""},"hp":{"details":"","max":155,"temp":0,"value":155},"resistances":[{"type":"mental","value":10}],"speed":{"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":20}],"value":20}},"details":{"blurb":"","languages":{"details":"tongues","value":["common"]},"level":{"value":9},"privateNotes":"","publicNotes":"<p>Rarely, when an ioton leeches a particularly secretive thought, it can choke to death on the secret, only to be born from its previous body into that of a loreavor: an ennosite whose existence is shaped around the consumption of secrets and artistry.</p>\n<p>Loreavors sip at secrets throughout their lives and are instinctively drawn to obscure information. Their hunger places them firmly at odds with scholars and historians alike. Living victims lose memories; written texts become blank books. Loreavors' favorite sites are ruins and ancient libraries, but they can also survive on banal secrets of everyday life as well. While the creatures are secretive, typically staying out of sight and fleeing danger, they become aggressive when their favored food sources are threatened.</p>\n<p>A loreavor appears as a 3-foot-long, pale, wormlike creature with dozens of half-formed faces growing from its segmented body. Trapped in an area without secrets to eat, a loreavor won't starve and can live for years.</p>","publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Shadows at Sundown"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"perception":{"details":"","mod":19,"senses":[{"acuity":"imprecise","range":60,"type":"thoughtsense"}]},"resources":{},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":15},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":21},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":19}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":19},"arcana":{"base":17},"occultism":{"base":21},"society":{"base":17},"stealth":{"base":19}},"traits":{"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"sm"},"value":["astral"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"npc","effects":[]},{"_id":"sawfqpGNObMA41at","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/npc.svg","items":["vhfIj6vLRTmu7IjN","iwkjPxza1YRU9xOM","PuHMfTpVX5nVaVQb","wgMOFOmkU54gtQeG","jwssM4TlBY6RdPNC","cse9qAgtS3C67Qxb"],"name":"Ileosa's Shell","system":{"abilities":{"cha":{"mod":0},"con":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":0},"str":{"mod":8},"wis":{"mod":5}},"attributes":{"ac":{"details":"","value":34},"allSaves":{"value":""},"hp":{"details":"void healing","max":235,"temp":0,"value":235},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed"},{"type":"death-effects"},{"type":"disease"},{"type":"mental"},{"type":"paralyzed"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"unconscious"}],"resistances":[{"exceptions":["silver"],"type":"physical","value":10}],"speed":{"otherSpeeds":[],"value":25},"weaknesses":[{"type":"bleed","value":10}]},"details":{"blurb":"","languages":{"details":"(can't speak any language)","value":["aklo","common","diabolic","elven","jotun","shadowtongue","thassilonian","varisian"]},"level":{"value":13},"privateNotes":"","publicNotes":"","publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Shadows at Sundown"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"perception":{"details":"","mod":24,"senses":[{"type":"greater-darkvision"}]},"resources":{},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":22},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":26},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":24}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":24},"athletics":{"base":27}},"traits":{"rarity":"unique","size":{"value":"med"},"value":["evil","undead","unholy"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"npc","effects":[]},{"_id":"wCztuDEePLs9ZsEl","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/npc.svg","items":["VNiOGGKc54QUfVbN","Ny3NqbCBZzlv4JM1","xOAww92oLwE2bFGP","iEpl1ftFcGwfzBrj","btTBBVcEn1QoMNoy","yKYtmjAiJssqC7aa","p76eWhT6p9KKMFHn","mMCVlK9voS7wE7Qu","djho22lA5aIk9m1t","SFUqEQbm7kpOQCMs","vWRcpO7j45ovpi5Z","3HkgAS4oM6Yz2NxU","Go3YVSkU8iq4ZTcn","CqieI7gO2HphJGdK","KgT0aNCwlMEVzqnm","XPFjlATV5vvpvbUh","Vm5M5rARJcJ1qBjs","BXAolSChSRtaW5bV","qbxqUljXeeUNsK8S","sCnhcZGec7t2b6Io","lHx1Txb2tJ6AtflG","treG00Et9eKWUzLb","0VZiX0wgmyt0qUkk","4tLn3hfHT9BgMqV5","OO0fehfzRpRCk1dM","5ATjksoW7V9N9XPa","GvMoKZWw2PLoariE","pbddjh9dwb5aH6Fx","UD9ytc6uy8m6CEM9","6ByGBm17u9v8v1LU","hocCiVlrTXtJKh1B","QW6YkTROI7Y3Hliw","T40OeGM6GGMYF1OQ","f8m2RRIv5Tl9viCs","HG44xugoCR6oqKO8","8OsjKz1WLqrKF8au","1YRJzF3w6jxOH5vf","vuFw3gBVrRC2amVY","S3UbnqRRcnn1Jbmp","wh3xNTBFNNs0L2PV","fjZc2tqzo5wboCNx","UXMpegXgDFumQ7kR","hCwxsYrYChQQOhLP","jTPiUcXPtiMhrrcE","tLOrZubd2t1vodQ4","DgrHRQSVPvwvmbNB","xYMEN3kfGAaLgbsU","c0ANnD74wARRjHiD","vFlYJdySuAhicXMk","o8WobYB2H5s1BYho","tddsy5Ng0iM3EqZx","oUowrBkgg74TlRMs","6BgNKyiG87Xp5LWY","FuYEZjBTElBUIc4q","37EVCGPfSFZ6mKY9"],"name":"Strigoi Progenitor","system":{"abilities":{"cha":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":5},"str":{"mod":8},"wis":{"mod":4}},"attributes":{"ac":{"details":"","value":34},"allSaves":{"value":""},"hp":{"details":"coffin restoration, fast healing 10, void healing","max":180,"temp":0,"value":180},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects"},{"type":"disease"},{"type":"paralyzed"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"sleep"}],"speed":{"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":25}],"value":25}},"details":{"blurb":"","languages":{"details":"","value":["common","necril","shadowtongue","thassilonian"]},"level":{"value":13},"privateNotes":"","publicNotes":"<p>The most powerful strigoi are those intentionally summoned into the bodies of willing hosts in times long past. As the rites to do so are lost to time, very few strigoi progenitors exist today. Those who do trace their lives back well over ten thousand years ago to Thassilon, Azlant, or similar ancient empires. A strigoi progenitor may appear to possess the vitality of the living, yet closer inspection reveals sharp fangs, the faintest smell of decay, and the strange and unsettling shifting of their shadow. In life, this example strigoi progenitor was a powerful oracle and advisor in Runelord Sorshen's nation of Eurythnia.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The oldest of all vampires are the strigoi. They predate ancient nosferatus and view moroi as infantile children, yet their own origins are so far lost to the ravages of time that few today have heard of them and fewer still know their true nature. Many of the oldest tales about vampires trace back to the strigoi, and nearly every other vampire carries traits that ultimately have their roots in these powerful, ancient creatures.</p>\n<p>Strigoi, in their true form, are bodiless creatures native to the Shadow Plane that are incapable of interacting with the physical world, existing only as pure forces of malevolence. When this malevolence is invited into a physical body by method of ancient rituals, though, a strigoi becomes much more dangerous. This requirement-that a living creature perform a rite of their own free will to draw the strigoi into their soul-may well be the source of a moroi's compulsion not to enter a home without first being invited.</p>\n<p>Some myths point to Urgathoa as the source of the ritual that allowed spellcasters to become strigoi, while others suggest the method was spread by the cult of Zura. Whatever the source, this long-lost ritual was no gateway to power, but instead a trap that allowed the strigoi to inhabit the shadows and souls of once-living hosts. In so doing, they found a way to exist in the world of flesh and blood. The presence of a strigoi within the shadow of a living host causes sickness and swift death, after which the strigoi bonds with the host's soul and becomes one with the body. Thus did the first of their kind invade the world of the living, and thus did the first vampires walk the night.</p>","publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Shadows at Sundown"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"perception":{"details":"","mod":23,"senses":[{"type":"greater-darkvision"}]},"resources":{"focus":{"max":1,"value":1}},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":24},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":26},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":22}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":25},"arcana":{"base":23},"athletics":{"base":25},"crafting":{"base":23},"deception":{"base":26},"religion":{"base":22},"stealth":{"base":27}},"spellcasting":{"rituals":{"dc":33}},"traits":{"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"},"value":["evil","lawful","shadow","undead","unholy","vampire"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"npc","effects":[]},{"_id":"z03ztiH8vBDRQTuw","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/hazard.svg","items":["SoUjhknpCUBSa9Yd"],"name":"Paradox Engine","system":{"attributes":{"ac":{"value":36},"hardness":24,"hp":{"details":"","max":90,"temp":0,"value":90},"immunities":[{"type":"critical-hits"},{"type":"precision"}],"stealth":{"details":"","value":0}},"creatureType":"","details":{"description":"<p>All six sides of this adamantine-reinforced box are covered with Thassilonian runes. Touching a rune allows one to exchange its position with another.</p>","disable":"<p>@Check[thievery|dc:41] (expert) to feel the subtle vibrations when moving a rune to shift into the right position, or @Check[thassilon-lore|dc:33] (expert) or @Check[society|dc:38] (master) while being able to read Thassilonian to work out the anagram puzzle using traditional means, or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.9HpwDN4MYQJnW0LG]{Dispel Magic} (7th rank; counteract DC 34)</p>","isComplex":true,"level":{"value":14},"publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Adventure: Shadows at Sundown"},"reset":"<p>The paradox engine deactivates 1 minute, and its owb prophet returns to its interior after all creatures leave the area, but resets immediately thereafter.</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The slicing shadows congeal into the form of what appears to be the upper half of a skeletal, cowled humanoid: an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.pathfinder-monster-core-2.Actor.4NXlXj2looUjPJY1]{Owb Prophet}. This owb prophet is a creation of the paradox engine and does not have a forsaken patron. While the owb prophet is active, the paradox engine no longer uses its Slicing Shadows reaction; instead, the owb prophet focuses its attacks on creatures that attempt to damage or deactivate the engine. If the owb prophet is destroyed, the paradox engine's disable DCs and Hardness are reduced by 5. It thereafter functions as a simple hazard with the Slicing Shadows reaction, and resets after 1 round.</p>"},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":28},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":22},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":0}},"statusEffects":[],"traits":{"rarity":"unique","size":{"value":"med"},"value":["magical","trap"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"hazard","effects":[]}]